# Held whole-Init comparison proposal

This is Source preparation only. No Native result, candidate output or numerical
answer was read while preparing it. Root must supply actual released custody QA,
the recorded Native workflow, both candidate requests/builds/executions and the
actual formatted observer/API bindings. There is no guessed runtime identity.

The fixed lanes remain fifteen unchanged ordinary loader inputs and six literal
direct-state inputs. Their admission, order and conversion proofs are input
authorities. They are not selected from observed results. Native06 and its full
four-TU Init call remain independent of the Rust ordinary and direct APIs.

The runner uses the established exact comparison mechanism, existing recorder
and full-file hash checks, and the narrow two-lane JSON streaming adapter. It
retains every case, allocated row/tail, mismatch and unavailable obligation. The
existing 4 GiB per-file factual resource bound rejects excess without truncating,
sampling or changing input/run duration. Metadata limits do not cap result files.

Required pairs are declaration/order and actual invocation/return, the shared
1301 named registry indices and all allocated report/subtable/column/table slots,
all31 Scan scalar owners, reached report/progress order, actual backend counters
and flags at matching entry/exit stages, and source-supported public storage.
Allocated owner bounds and the one-based Native/zero-based Rust transport indices
are authenticated explicitly. Optional/unallocated owners retain their actual
null/empty distinction. Table original-real owners and public scalar DTOs compare
IEEE bits and class; optional decimal rendering is not a scientific operand.

Public storage keeps the six already frozen zero-tolerance/class/shape/signed-zero
profiles and eight exact positive-zero reset-array obligations, all19 slots.
Returned eligible owners missing on either or both sides fail. Declared excluded,
out-of-capacity, stopped or nonreturned branches remain unavailable and never PASS.
The comparer does not evaluate CTF, reports, Scan, default values or diagnostics.

Native AfterRegistry pairs with the direct Rust registry after its initial call;
Native BeforeRegistry can pair with a genuinely retained default caller owner.
Native BeforeInit and the actual endpoint pair with the corresponding direct
caller records. Production entry ownership spans thirteen Native loader calls
and one Rust typed compiler/initializer. Native BeforeRegistry pairs with the
actual Rust caller before its producer; Native production BeforeInit has no
matching retained Rust intermediate and is explicitly unpaired.

Native reached Init events supply report return order, actual Scan return, header
completion, final fatal boundary and normal whole-function return. Rust progress
copies supply their actual corresponding successful calls/return. No postlude
progress is inferred from a final count or from an exception message.

Production b089 preserves reports/backend/prefixes on error but drops unreturned
State/public storage. Those partial public/shared/aggregate owners are unavailable
there. The direct API retains these owners on error and can pair them with actual
Native public/caller events. No missing eligible returned owner is reclassified
as an excluded branch merely because the Rust initializer returned an error.

Native complete EIO/error/console files are always hashed and retained. Production
Native streams include loader prefixes absent from the Rust caller; no guessed
slice or header stripping creates byte parity. Dedicated direct complete EIO can
be compared literally where both actual callers own that complete stream. Error
headers use genuinely different caller version/IDD strings, which remain explicit
unpaired inputs. Ordered actual callback arguments/levels can pair in direct6;
b089 has no callbacks and makes no optional-backend parity claim.

Native registry22 real totals, component-size/shadow owners and DoPlantSizing are
full custody context: the selected Init/report suffix does not read or modify
them. Rust does not invent those owners. Native address values, implementation
exception type names, CurrentDateTime, optional SQLite/fMessage/OutUnit backends
and production header strings are likewise unpaired where no shared input owner
exists. Unpaired context is listed, not silently counted as a comparison.

Old09 all-visit mathematical handoffs remain separate existing comparisons; this
runner does not replay them or inherit a whole-Init PASS from them. The result
reports actionable mismatches and exact compared-owner coverage. Whole-Init,
production integration and full CTF10 gates remain false while required unpaired
or unavailable obligations remain. Root and another author must review the final
held runner before any execution.

The executable is `compare.py`, with eleven mandatory options:
`--approved-source-sha256` (the held manifest SHA), `--source-manifest`,
`--original-data-review`, `--original-data-review-execution`,
`--production-request`, `--production-build-execution`, `--production-execution`,
`--direct-request`, `--direct-build-execution`, `--direct-execution`, and
`--output-dir`. Every reference option uses actual `path#SHA256`; both build
options bind the same genuine locked two-example Cargo build. OriginalQA must
have completed and released custody before either candidate invocation.

The comparison requires the complete actual QA stdout, twelve Native sources,
all frozen input/conversion authorities, both actual argc3 observer calls and
the raw Cargo Source snapshot containing every current own/API source. The
held observer path inventories supply only source membership/order; actual
post-application hashes come from the genuine requests and Cargo archives.
No future formatted/runtime Source identity is synthesized here.

Seven Python bodies are the runtime Source closure. The exact prior packet IO
and Comparison class are retained; generic recorder custody and the top-level
stream adapter are bounded adaptations. The three new bodies join actual
owners/stages and emit full mismatch/availability records. No executable test,
project import, Native/Rust numerical output or target was used during preparation.
